            'visa_subclass_code' => null,
            'intro_html' => '<p>Most sources say Indian ordinary-passport holders need Iraq\'s mandatory e-Visa (via evisa.iq) before travel, generally for a 30-day stay, though figures on the fee and processing time conflict and one outlier source claims visa-free entry. No dedicated, bilateral India-Iraq family-residence scheme was found for federal Iraq. The one officially documented family-residence route located is specific to the Kurdistan Region of Iraq: a spousal residency card issued under Foreigners Residency Law No. 76 of 2017, where one spouse must be an Iraqi citizen. Iraq\'s security situation is a separate matter from these formal visa/residency rules and is not addressed here.</p>',
