            'authority_url' => 'https://security-legislation.ly/?p=19579',
            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Eligibility rests on the SPONSOR already holding valid Libyan work and residency permits.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Sponsor Requirements</h4><ul><li>Must hold valid Libyan work and residency permits</li><li>Must demonstrate sufficient financial means to support dependants, per secondary guidance</li><li>Typically files the dependant\'s entry-visa application through their employer, with the Ministry of Interior</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Dependants Covered (per Law No. 17 of 1962)</h4><ul><li>Wife</li><li>Minor children</li><li>Unmarried daughters</li><li>Dependent parents</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Registration Duty</h4><p>Dependants named on an entry visa must register with the passports authority within 7 days of arrival, per Law No. 6 of 1987 as reported.</p><p>This eligibility summary is limited to the formal family-residency framework and does not address Libya\'s separately disclosed security/diplomatic situation.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who Applies</h4><p>Your sponsor (commonly via their employer) typically files the entry-visa application for you from Libya with the Ministry of Interior; you then register with the passports authority and apply for your residency permit after arrival.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Documents You Will Likely Need</h4><ul><li>Valid Indian passport</li><li>Marriage certificate (spouse) or birth certificate (child/dependent parent relationship), legalised as required</li><li>Proof of the sponsor\'s financial means</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>What Your Sponsor Will Need</h4><p>Their own valid Libyan work and residency permits, filed typically through their employer.</p><p>Given the thin and conflicting secondary guidance available, and separate from Libya\'s security/diplomatic situation disclosed elsewhere in this project, we strongly recommend confirming current requirements directly with the Libyan embassy/consulate serving India before proceeding.</p>',
