            'biometric_status' => 'conditional',
            'interview_status' => 'required',
            'official_visa_name' => 'Family Reunification Residence Permit (Liechtenstein), via Swiss National (D) Visa lodged at the Embassy of Switzerland, New Delhi',
            'visa_subclass_code' => null,
            'intro_html' => 'Liechtenstein has no diplomatic mission in India, so an Indian spouse, registered partner or dependant joining a Liechtenstein-based sponsor must first obtain a Schengen national (D) visa at the Embassy of Switzerland in New Delhi, while the actual family-reunification residence permit is decided separately by Liechtenstein\'s own Migration and Passport Office (Ausländer- und Passamt, APA). A married spouse or registered partner of a sponsor holding a B, C or D residence permit has a materially clearer path than an unmarried partner, for whom there is no automatic entitlement.',
            'typical_stay' => 'Residence permit renewable in line with the sponsor\'s own permit; the initial Swiss national D visa is generally issued for a single entry to enable relocation, not for a fixed tourist-style stay',
            'entry_type' => 'Single-entry national (D) visa for relocation, followed by an APA-issued Liechtenstein residence permit (this is not a Schengen short-stay family-visit visa)',
            'processing_time_text' => 'Not independently confirmed. The final decision on the residence permit rests with Liechtenstein\'s APA, not the Swiss Embassy, and no fixed timeline was found in the sources reviewed; applicants should plan for several weeks to a few months',
