            'application_method' => 'The Liechtenstein-based sponsor files the family-reunification request with the Migration and Passport Office (APA) in Liechtenstein at least 4 weeks before the planned move; the Indian family member separately books a VFS Global appointment and lodges the national (D) visa application in person at the Embassy of Switzerland, New Delhi',
            'interview_required' => 'Required - in-person lodgement at the Swiss Embassy\'s Visa Section (Chanakyapuri) is mandatory; no postal or online lodgement was described in the sources reviewed',
            'biometric_required' => 'Not independently confirmed for the national D visa itself; Schengen short-stay (C) visas processed by the same visa section require biometric enrolment, so a similar requirement is plausible but unconfirmed here',
            'government_fee_text' => 'A 2020-2023 Swiss family-reunion visa checklist for the wider region quoted an adult visa fee of around EUR 80; this is dated and should be reconfirmed directly with the Swiss Embassy, New Delhi, before applying',
            'application_centre' => 'Embassy of Switzerland, Visa Section, Chanakyapuri, New Delhi (appointment via VFS Global); the residence-permit decision itself is made by the APA in Liechtenstein, not in India',
            'authority_name' => 'Migration and Passport Office (Ausländer- und Passamt), Principality of Liechtenstein',
            'authority_url' => 'https://www.llv.li/en/national-administration/migration-and-passport-office/family-reunification/residence-permit-for-partner',
            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Family reunification in Liechtenstein depends first on the sponsor\'s own residence status, and second on whether the Indian applicant is a spouse/registered partner or an unmarried partner.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Sponsor Status Required</h4><ul><li>Non-EEA, non-Swiss sponsors (for example, an Indian or other third-country national already settled in Liechtenstein) must hold a B, C or D residence permit before they can bring family members in</li><li>Swiss and EEA national sponsors holding a Liechtenstein residence permit can have family join at any time, under broader rules not covered here</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who Qualifies as a Dependant</h4><ul><li>Spouse or registered partner</li><li>Joint unmarried children under 18</li><li>Unmarried (de facto) life partners are NOT treated the same as spouses - they fall under a separate, discretionary route, not an automatic entitlement</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Unmarried Partners - A Different, Harder Route</h4><p>This route requires a duly certified long-term relationship, a bank guarantee from an EEA-area bank, and proof of no dependence on social assistance. Per the Migration and Passport Office, there is no entitlement to a residence permit for a civil/unmarried partnership - each case is assessed at the authority\'s discretion.</p><p>This is general guidance, not a guarantee of approval - every application is individually assessed by Liechtenstein\'s Migration and Passport Office (APA).</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who Applies, and Where</h4><p>Two separate steps are involved: your Liechtenstein-based sponsor files the family-reunification request with the APA in Liechtenstein, while you independently book a VFS Global appointment and lodge your national (D) visa application in person at the Embassy of Switzerland, New Delhi.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Documents You Will Need</h4><ul><li>Valid passport</li><li>Personal cover letter and an invitation letter from your sponsor</li><li>Original Indian marriage certificate issued by the Registrar of Marriages, legalized by the relevant State Home Ministry, and then further legalized by the Ministry of External Affairs, New Delhi (a marriage deed alone is reported as not accepted)</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>What Your Sponsor Must Provide</h4><p>A copy of their Liechtenstein residence/work permit and passport, proof of accommodation, and - for unmarried partners only - a bank guarantee from an EEA-area bank plus evidence of a long-term relationship.</p><p>Our consultants can help you sequence the APA filing in Liechtenstein with your parallel visa application at the Swiss Embassy in New Delhi.</p>',
            'seo_title' => 'Liechtenstein Family Visa for Indians | Reunification',
            'meta_description' => 'Joining family in Liechtenstein from India? Understand the Swiss Embassy D-visa route, APA sponsor rules and documents needed, via VisaAgency.in.',
            'og_title' => 'Liechtenstein Family Reunification Route for Indians',
            'og_description' => 'Liechtenstein has no mission in India - family reunification runs via the Swiss Embassy, New Delhi, and Liechtenstein\'s own Migration and Passport Office. Here is how it works.',
            'documents' => [
