            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who Applies, and in What Order</h4><p>The family-reunification request is normally filed with the Directorate of Immigration before you travel - either by your sponsor or by you. Only after that request is approved do you apply for the entry (D) visa via the Luxembourg Visa Application Centre (VFS Global) in India, followed by an in-person residence-card application at the commune of residence within 3 months of arriving in Luxembourg.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Documents You Will Need</h4><ul><li>Valid passport (at least 3 months\' validity beyond the planned stay)</li><li>Proof of the marital relationship (marriage certificate)</li><li>Medical examination and tuberculosis screening results (required for third-country nationals applying for a residence permit exceeding 3 months)</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>What Your Sponsor Must Separately Show</h4><p>Your sponsor\'s stable, regular income (benchmarked to the unskilled minimum wage over 12 months) and suitable accommodation are assessed as part of the reunification request - these are the sponsor\'s requirements, distinct from your own relationship and medical documents.</p><p>Our consultants can help you and your sponsor sequence the Directorate of Immigration filing correctly before you apply for the entry visa.</p>',
