            'official_visa_name' => 'Temporary Residency - Family Dependent Application/Extension (IPIM), for family of a Macau temporary resident; short visits use ordinary visa-free/visa-on-arrival entry, not a distinct family-visit visa',
            'visa_subclass_code' => null,
            'intro_html' => 'Macau SAR has no separate short-stay "family visit visa" distinct from its general entry rules - Indian nationals already enter visa-free (reportedly for short tourist stays, commonly cited as up to 30 days, though sources conflict on the exact figure and process for longer stays). For a longer-term family stay, the applicable route is a "family dependent" application or extension under Macau\'s Temporary Residency system, administered by the Macao Trade and Investment Promotion Institute (IPIM), which attaches a spouse, minor child or other recognized dependant to a Macau temporary resident sponsor (for example, an investor, or management/technical/skilled-worker permit holder) rather than being a free-standing family visa.',
