            'official_visa_name' => 'Moldova Family Reunification Temporary Residence (GIM/BMA Notification + Type D Visa)',
            'visa_subclass_code' => null,
            'intro_html' => '<p>Moldova has no single, standalone \'Family Visa\' for Indian nationals. Short family visits generally use the ordinary Type C visa for tourism or visiting relatives/friends (up to 90 days in 180). Longer-term family reunification is a separate two-stage process under Law 200/2010: a sponsor already living in Moldova (a Moldovan citizen or a foreigner with temporary/permanent residence) first files a \'notification of family reunification\' with the migration authority, and only after that is approved does the Indian family member apply for a Type D long-stay visa, followed by registration for a temporary residence permit after arrival.</p>',
            'typical_stay' => 'Type C family-visit route: up to 90 days in any 180-day period. Family-reunification route: third-party reporting (not an official page) describes an initial temporary residence period of around 12 months, renewable while the relationship and the sponsor\'s own status continue.',
            'entry_type' => 'Type C family-visit visa can be single or multiple-entry depending on what is issued. The Type D long-stay visa used for family reunification is generally single-entry for the initial entry; the residence permit that follows is a status, not an entry type.',
