            'validity_text' => 'Temporary residence permit reported by non-official sources as valid for about 1 year and renewable. Not independently confirmed on an official Moldovan government page in this research pass.',
            'application_method' => 'Two stages: (1) the Moldova-based sponsor files a notification of family reunification with the migration authority (GIM/BMA); (2) once approved, the Indian family member applies for a Type D long-stay visa at the Moldovan Embassy/Consulate covering India, then registers in Moldova for the temporary residence permit. A short Type C family-visit visa, where that route is used instead, is applied for directly at the Moldovan mission or via the e-visa portal (evisa.gov.md) for eligible applicants.',
