            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Eligibility depends on who the Moldova-based sponsor is and what status they hold.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who the Sponsor Can Be</h4><ul><li>A Moldovan citizen, or</li><li>A foreigner already holding a valid Moldovan temporary or permanent residence permit</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Eligible Family Members</h4><ul><li>Spouse</li><li>Minor children (born in or out of marriage, or adopted)</li><li>Unmarried adult children who cannot support themselves for medical reasons</li><li>Dependent parents</li><li>Persons under guardianship</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Unmarried Partners — Narrow Recognition</h4><p>Moldova recognises an unmarried \'partner\' only where the sponsor is a Moldovan citizen, the partner is unmarried, and the couple is cohabiting with at least one shared child. This partner route does not appear to extend to partners of foreign residence-permit holders based on the official documents found. Same-sex partners/spouses are not addressed in the sources found — not independently confirmed either way.</p><p>This is general guidance, not a guarantee of approval; every case is individually assessed by Moldovan migration authorities.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who Applies, and Where</h4><p>Your Moldova-based sponsor (spouse, parent, or partner, as applicable) first files the family-reunification notification inside Moldova. Only after that notification is approved do you apply for the Type D long-stay visa at the Moldovan Embassy/Consulate covering India.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Relationship & Civil-Status Documents</h4><ul><li>Marriage certificate (for a spouse) — must be transcribed into the Moldovan Civil Register</li><li>Birth certificate (for a child applicant), transcribed into the Moldovan Civil Register</li><li>Civil-status certificates (single/divorced/widowed) for both the applicant and the sponsor, where applicable</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Translation & Authentication</h4><p>Documents issued in India (criminal record, civil-status certificates) generally need to be apostilled and translated into Romanian before submission — confirm the current requirement with GIM/BMA, as requirements can change.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Joint Presence</h4><p>For the partner-with-child category specifically, one official checklist states both family members must be present together when the documents are submitted.</p><p>Our consultants can help confirm which sponsor category and document checklist applies to your specific relationship before you approach the Moldovan mission.</p>',
