            'intro_html' => '<p>Monaco issues no visa of its own and has no border control separate from France. An Indian national visiting or joining family in Monaco applies for the ordinary French Schengen visa (short-stay Type C for a family visit, or a French long-stay visa for settling with family) at the French Embassy/Consulate in India, exactly as for mainland France. No Monaco-specific family-visa checklist was found under this same French process in this research pass — Monaco instead layers its own residency authorisation on top of the French visa for anyone intending to live there.</p>',
            'typical_stay' => 'Short family visit: standard Schengen short-stay limit, up to 90 days in any 180-day period. Settling with family in Monaco: a French long-stay visa followed by a Monaco resident card (carte de séjour monégasque), not a fixed short stay.',
