            'authority_name' => 'French Embassy/Consulate in India; Monegasque immigration authorities',
            'authority_url' => null,
            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Eligibility for the visa stage follows the ordinary French Schengen family-visit or family-of-French/family-of-foreign-resident rules, since Monaco has no separate visa system.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Short Family Visit</h4><p>An Indian national visiting a relative resident in Monaco applies for a Schengen Type C visa through the French Embassy/Consulate in India, generally supported by an invitation/accommodation document from the Monaco-resident host.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Settling with a Monaco-Resident Spouse/Family Member</h4><p>One specialised source describes this as requiring a settlement visa before a Monaco resident card can be issued to the joining spouse, with proof of accommodation in Monaco from the sponsoring resident. This is not a standardised, India-specific \'family visa\' — it is a case-by-case settlement process layered on top of the French visa.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Unmarried/Registered Partners</h4><p>Not independently confirmed — no Monaco- or France-specific guidance distinguishing unmarried-partner treatment for a Monaco-bound case was found in this research pass.</p><p>This is general guidance, not a guarantee of approval.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Where You Apply</h4><p>You apply at the French Embassy/Consulate (or VFS France centre) in India, the same channel used for mainland-France Schengen visas, since Monaco has no consular presence of its own for visa issuance.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Documents Typically Expected</h4><ul><li>Valid passport</li><li>Proof of relationship to the Monaco-resident family member (marriage/birth certificate)</li><li>Evidence of the sponsor\'s Monaco residence status and accommodation</li><li>Standard Schengen supporting documents (travel insurance, return ticket, financial means)</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>For Settlement Cases</h4><p>If you intend to live in Monaco permanently with a resident spouse or family member, expect an additional settlement-authorisation step with the Monegasque authorities, on top of the French visa — this is not confirmed to have a simple fixed checklist in this research pass.</p><p>Our consultants can help you clarify whether your case is a short family visit or a settlement case, and which document set applies.</p>',
