            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Eligibility is defined by sponsor type and relationship, with the clearest official category being for spouses of Mongolian citizens.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>F1 — Spouse of a Mongolian National</h4><p>For a foreign national (including an Indian citizen) married to a Mongolian citizen. Requires an invitation letter from the Mongolian spouse, the spouse\'s ID, an officially translated marriage certificate, proof of sufficient funds, a police clearance certificate from the country of origin, and a health test report.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>F1-1, F3, F3-1 — Other Family of a Mongolian National</h4><p>Cover family members of the F1 spouse and children of a Mongolian national, per the Immigration Agency\'s category list; detailed document requirements for these sub-categories were not independently confirmed in this research pass.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Spouse/Child of a Foreign (Non-Mongolian) Resident</h4><p>No confirmed Permit-F category was found covering an Indian spouse joining a foreign resident of Mongolia who is not a Mongolian citizen. A separate \'G\'-type permit appears to cover a residence permit for an immigrant\'s (permanent-residence holder\'s) child, but this was not independently confirmed as extending to spouses. Treat this as an open gap — confirm directly with the Immigration Agency of Mongolia.</p><p>This is general guidance, not a guarantee of approval.</p>',
