            'official_visa_name' => 'New Caledonia Family Visa (via France-Visas, New Caledonia Selected — Not Standard Schengen)',
            'visa_subclass_code' => null,
            'intro_html' => '<p>New Caledonia is a French sui generis overseas collectivity outside the Schengen Area, with its own entry rules — confirmed again here, consistent with an earlier Medical Visa phase of this project. The official New Caledonia tourism authority confirms a 24-consecutive-hour visa-exempt stopover rule that explicitly names India among the exempt nationalities. Beyond a stopover, family reunification works through the ordinary France-Visas system with New Caledonia specifically selected as the destination (not the mainland/Schengen wizard), either as a short-stay visit or, for settling with a sponsor already holding a long-stay visa and New Caledonia work permit, a family-reunification long-stay visa.</p>',
            'typical_stay' => 'Visa-exempt stopover: under 24 consecutive hours only. Short-stay family visit (beyond the stopover): up to 90 days in 180, per general short-stay exemption/visa rules reported for New Caledonia. Long-stay family reunification: tied to the sponsor\'s long-stay visa/work-permit validity, not a fixed short-stay period.',
            'entry_type' => 'Stopover exemption: not a visa at all, limited to under 24 hours and not usable for a family stay. Beyond that, a short-stay visa (where required) or a long-stay family-reunification visa, selected via France-Visas for the New Caledonia destination specifically.',
