            'validity_text' => 'Not independently confirmed for the New Caledonia-specific family-reunification long-stay visa; tied to the sponsor\'s own long-stay visa and work-permit validity per one non-official source.',
            'application_method' => 'Apply via France-Visas, explicitly selecting New Caledonia as the destination (not the default mainland-France/Schengen path), at the French Embassy/Consulate or VFS France centre in India. For family reunification specifically, the New Caledonia-based sponsor must already hold a valid long-stay visa and a New Caledonia work permit before the family member\'s application can proceed, per a non-official guide; a separate precedent (a New Caledonia administrative court ruling) also describes a \'famille de Français\' (family of a French national) long-stay visa route for a spouse of a French citizen residing in New Caledonia.',
            'interview_required' => 'Not independently confirmed',
            'biometric_required' => 'Not independently confirmed for the New Caledonia-specific process; likely consistent with standard French long-stay visa biometric enrolment, but not confirmed as identical to mainland Schengen rules given New Caledonia\'s separate status.',
            'government_fee_text' => 'Not independently confirmed for New Caledonia specifically in this research pass.',
            'application_centre' => 'France-Visas (New Caledonia destination selected), via the French Embassy/Consulate or VFS France centre serving India; local formalities are completed with the French High Commission in New Caledonia (Haut-Commissariat) after arrival.',
            'authority_name' => 'France-Visas / Haut-Commissariat de la République en Nouvelle-Calédonie',
            'authority_url' => 'https://www.newcaledonia.travel/pro/promoting-the-archipelago/thematic-fact-sheets/visa-passport-and-entry-requirements/',
            'eligibility_html' => '<p><strong>Stopover exemption is not a family-stay route:</strong> the official New Caledonia tourism page confirms Indian passport holders are visa-exempt for a stopover of under 24 consecutive hours — useful only for a transit, never for actually visiting or joining family.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Short Family Visit (Beyond the Stopover)</h4><p>Likely uses a short-stay visa process selected via France-Visas for New Caledonia specifically; not confirmed to be identical to the mainland Schengen short-stay family-visit rules given New Caledonia\'s separate, non-Schengen status.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Family Reunification (Long-Stay)</h4><p>A non-official guide describes this as available to the spouse and minor children of a sponsor who already holds a valid New Caledonia long-stay visa and work permit, with the sponsor expected to show sufficient income and suitable housing.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Family of a French Citizen</h4><p>A separate, concrete precedent exists: a documented New Caledonia administrative court case describes a foreign spouse of a French citizen entering on a short-stay visa, marrying locally, then returning on a long-stay \'famille de Français\' visa — a distinct route from the general work-permit-holder family-reunification route above.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Unmarried Partners</h4><p>Not independently confirmed for the New Caledonia-specific process.</p><p>This is general guidance, not a guarantee of approval; confirm current rules with France-Visas (New Caledonia selected) and the French High Commission in New Caledonia.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Select New Caledonia, Not Mainland France</h4><p>When using France-Visas, explicitly select New Caledonia as your destination rather than assuming the standard Schengen wizard applies — New Caledonia is outside Schengen with its own rules.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Sponsor Requirements (Kept Separate From Yours)</h4><ul><li>Valid New Caledonia long-stay visa and work permit (for the general family-reunification route), or French citizenship and New Caledonia residence (for the \'famille de Français\' route)</li><li>Sufficient income and suitable housing</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Your Documents as the Applicant</h4><ul><li>Marriage or birth certificate proving the relationship</li><li>Standard long-stay visa supporting documents</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Note on Stopovers</h4><p>If you are only transiting through New Caledonia for under 24 hours, the visa-exempt stopover rule applies, but this cannot be used to visit or join family — a full visa application is required for that.</p><p>Our consultants can help you select the correct France-Visas pathway for New Caledonia and confirm which family route (general work-permit-holder reunification vs \'famille de Français\') fits your case.</p>',
