            'authority_url' => null,
            'eligibility_html' => '<p><strong>Baseline entry-visa conflict (disclosed):</strong> most sources checked say Indian citizens need a visa to enter Niger, obtained in person at the Embassy of Niger in New Delhi; one outlier source claims visa-free entry for 30-90 days, which could not be verified and should not be relied on.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>No Distinct Family/Dependent Category Found</h4><p>Despite a targeted search, no Niger-specific family-reunification or dependent-visa category, sponsor-residence requirement, or income/accommodation threshold was returned by search in this research pass. This appears to be a genuine evidence gap rather than confirmation that no such process exists — it may simply not be documented online in sources accessible via WebSearch.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Yellow Fever Certificate</h4><p>Multiple sources agree a yellow fever vaccination certificate is mandatory for entry to Niger, which would apply to a family visit as much as to tourism or business.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Travel-Advisory Caveat</h4><p>One source notes that most governments have advised against travel to Niger following the July 2023 coup — relevant context for anyone planning a family visit, independent of the visa process itself.</p><p>This is general guidance, not a guarantee of approval; confirm current requirements and any family-specific provision directly with the Embassy of Niger in New Delhi.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>No Confirmed Family-Specific Process</h4><p>Based on the evidence found, you would apply for Niger\'s ordinary visa at the Embassy of the Republic of Niger in New Delhi, rather than a separate family/dependent visa — no such distinct category was located in this research pass.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Documents Likely Needed</h4><ul><li>Valid passport (at least 6 months\' validity reported by one source)</li><li>Yellow fever vaccination certificate (mandatory per multiple sources)</li><li>Family invitation letter (not confirmed as a formal requirement, but a reasonable supporting document for a family-purpose visit)</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Recommended Next Step</h4><p>Given the absence of confirmed family-specific provisions, we recommend contacting the Embassy of the Republic of Niger in New Delhi directly to ask whether any family-reunification or dependent category exists beyond the ordinary visa.</p><p>Our consultants can help you prepare that enquiry and the ordinary-visa application in the meantime.</p>',
