            'intro_html' => '<p>Nigeria genuinely separates two routes that are often confused. For an Indian spouse of a Nigerian citizen who wants to live in Nigeria, the Nigeria Immigration Service (NIS) publishes a specifically named Spouse of Nigerian Citizen Visa (N1A) on immigration.gov.ng, issued under Section 37(10) of the Immigration Act 2015. For an Indian relative who only wants to visit family in Nigeria short-term, the applicable category is the general Visiting Visa, issued as either F6A (single entry) or F6B (multiple entry, subject to reciprocity), not a family-specific code.</p>',
