            'application_centre' => 'Nigerian High Commission, New Delhi, or online via the NIS e-Visa portal.',
            'authority_name' => 'Nigeria Immigration Service (NIS)',
            'authority_url' => 'https://immigration.gov.ng/spouse-of-nigerian-citizen-visa-n1a/',
            'eligibility_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Spouse Route (N1A)</h4><p>For an Indian national married to a Nigerian citizen. Per the NIS page, required documents include a passport valid at least 6 months, a passport photo, an attested marriage certificate, a copy of the sponsor’s (Nigerian spouse’s) ID, proof of stable residence in Nigeria, and a police clearance certificate. The visa is described as barring employment and limiting the holder to living in Nigeria.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Short Family-Visit Route (F6A/F6B)</h4><p>For a relative visiting family or friends in Nigeria without intending to reside. Requires an invitation letter from the host (family/friend) in Nigeria who accepts ‘immigration responsibility’, a copy of the host’s Nigerian passport or residence permit, proof of funds (NIS references a 180-day bank statement), and a return ticket. F6B additionally requires that the invitation letter specifically request multiple entries, and is granted on a reciprocity basis tied to what Nigeria’s mission assesses India as offering Nigerian nationals.</p><p>No dependent-children-specific family visa code (distinct from N1A) was found in search results; children of a Nigerian-citizen spouse may fall under a related but unconfirmed category — verify directly with NIS or the High Commission.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who Applies</h4><p>For N1A, the Indian spouse applies, submitting the marriage certificate and the Nigerian spouse’s supporting documents. For F6A/F6B, the Indian relative applies, but the Nigeria-based host/family member must first issue the invitation letter accepting immigration responsibility.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Documents You Will Likely Need</h4><ul><li>Passport valid at least 6 months</li><li>Passport-size photograph</li><li>For N1A: attested marriage certificate, police clearance certificate, proof of the Nigerian spouse’s stable residence</li><li>For F6A/F6B: invitation letter from the host, host’s ID/passport copy, proof of funds, return ticket</li></ul><p>Document translation/legalisation requirements were not independently confirmed in search results — ask the Nigerian High Commission whether an attested (vs merely notarised) Indian marriage certificate is required.</p>',
