            'authority_name' => 'Servicio Nacional de Migración (SNM), Panama',
            'authority_url' => 'https://www.migracion.gob.pa/wp-content/uploads/02.DEPENDIENTE_DE_RESIDENTE_PERMANENTE.pdf',
            'eligibility_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Sponsor Requirements</h4><p>The sponsor must be a 2-year provisional resident, a permanent resident, or a Panamanian national (per SNM’s Article 224 reference). The sponsor must provide a notarised letter accepting responsibility and repatriation for the dependant, and a copy of their own residence card.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who Counts as a Dependant</h4><ul><li>Foreign spouse</li><li>Children under 18</li><li>Children 18–25, if studying regularly and economically dependent on the sponsor</li><li>Relatives with disabilities</li><li>Dependent parents</li><li>A minor under the sponsor’s demonstrated legal guardianship</li></ul><p>No separate unmarried-partner category was found in the official SNM checklist for this specific permit — only spouse, children, disabled relatives, and dependent parents are named.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Entry-Visa Caveat</h4><p>Separately and critically, note that the Mumbai consulate’s suspension of stamped tourist visas since November 2022 may or may not also affect the stamped visa needed to travel to Panama to begin this residence process — this was not independently confirmed and should be checked directly with the Consulate General of Panama in Mumbai or the SNM before planning travel.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Applicant (Dependant) Documents</h4><ul><li>Notarised power of attorney and application</li><li>Three photographs</li><li>Certified copy of passport</li><li>Criminal record certificate</li><li>Health certificate</li><li>Sworn personal-background declaration form</li><li>Proof of kinship (marriage certificate, birth certificate, or guardianship record), per SNM’s ‘Constancia de parentesco’ requirement</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Translation/Legalisation</h4><p>Not independently confirmed in full detail for this specific permit, though Indian civil documents (marriage/birth certificates) would typically need certified translation into Spanish and apostille/legalisation — confirm the exact requirement with SNM or a Panama immigration lawyer.</p><p>Remember to separately resolve the entry-visa question given the Mumbai consulate suspension before relying on being able to travel to Panama to file this application in person.</p>',
