            'intro_html' => '<p>Papua New Guinea’s Immigration and Citizenship Authority (ICA) publishes a specifically named Dependent of Papua New Guinea Citizen (Non-Working) visa for spouses and dependants of a PNG citizen who want to live in PNG temporarily. A related but distinct route exists for dependants of PNG permanent residents or Resident (Long Term) permit holders, where the dependant entry permit is tied to the principal applicant’s permit and must generally be included at the time of the principal’s initial application. No evidence was found of a separate short-stay “family visit” visa category distinct from PNG’s general visitor-visa rules for Indian nationals — sources also conflicted on whether Indian passport holders currently need a visa to enter PNG at all for ordinary visits, so that general entry question should be confirmed separately from the dependant-route question addressed here.</p>',
